<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ramon Berenguer III of Barcelona</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1082–1131</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Ramon Berenguer the Great</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ramon Berenguer III, called the Great, was count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a> from 1086 to 1131. He gained <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/besalu">Besalú</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cerdanya">Cerdanya</a> by inheritance and, through his marriage to Douce in 1112, the County of Provence. With <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pisa">Pisa</a> he led a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">crusade</a> against Muslim <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mallorca">Majorca</a> in 1114 to 1115, sacking the island before withdrawing. He became a Templar shortly before his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ramon-berenguer-iii-of-barcelona.jpg" alt="Ramon Berenguer III of Barcelona" width="207" height="347" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ramon_Berenguer_IV_(Barcelona).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
